{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\_cls6_jpg\\eng\\035.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "In 1913 Keller began lecturingwith the aid of an", "conf": 0.906, "box": [[73, 205], [664, 200], [664, 230], [74, 235]]}, {"text": "interpreter-worldwide on the needs of the blind. She spoke", "conf": 0.924, "box": [[74, 245], [790, 238], [790, 267], [75, 274]]}, {"text": "primarily on behalf of the Foundation for the Blind, for which", "conf": 0.912, "box": [[75, 283], [795, 271], [796, 303], [76, 316]]}, {"text": "she raised funds.", "conf": 0.866, "box": [[75, 324], [277, 318], [277, 348], [76, 354]]}, {"text": "In 1920, Keller started her campaign to bring improvement in", "conf": 0.92, "box": [[75, 360], [803, 353], [803, 383], [76, 390]]}, {"text": "the life of the deaf and blind. She also prompted the", "conf": 0.931, "box": [[76, 400], [702, 393], [703, 422], [77, 429]]}, {"text": "organisation of commissions for the blind in 30 U.S. states by", "conf": 0.944, "box": [[77, 438], [804, 426], [805, 462], [78, 474]]}, {"text": "1937.", "conf": 0.8, "box": [[78, 479], [147, 479], [147, 511], [78, 511]]}, {"text": "Besides giving lectures, Keller was a prolific writer during her", "conf": 0.927, "box": [[77, 518], [800, 508], [800, 539], [78, 550]]}, {"text": "lifetime. Her books include'The Story of My Life' and", "conf": 0.873, "box": [[78, 558], [710, 549], [711, 579], [79, 587]]}, {"text": "Optimism'(both 1903),'The World 1 Live In (1908),'Out of", "conf": 0.867, "box": [[82, 597], [782, 589], [782, 618], [83, 626]]}, {"text": "the Dark (1913), 'Midstream: My Later Life' (1929), \"Helen", "conf": 0.855, "box": [[78, 635], [761, 630], [761, 660], [79, 665]]}, {"text": "Keller's Journal' (1938), and 'Let Us Have Faith' (1940).", "conf": 0.941, "box": [[79, 674], [715, 670], [715, 699], [80, 703]]}, {"text": "Keller died in Westport, Connecticut, on June 1, 1968.", "conf": 0.925, "box": [[78, 712], [714, 709], [714, 739], [79, 742]]}, {"text": "Althoughherownlifewasoneof silenceanddarkness,He